.TH MXFS 5 "2026-03-10" "MXFS 0.10.0" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
mxfs \- Multinode XFS shared/clustered filesystem
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mount \-t mxfs
.RI [ \-o
.IR options ]
.I device directory
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mxfs
is a high-performance clustered filesystem that enables concurrent
multi-node read/write access to a single shared block device.  It reads
and writes the XFS on-disk format directly through its own DLM-aware
caching engine, delivering native XFS compatibility with full cluster
coordination.
.PP
MXFS is implemented as a single Linux kernel module
.RB ( mxfs.ko )
with no userspace daemon required.  All cluster coordination
(distributed locking, peer discovery, lease management, heartbeating,
and fencing) runs in-kernel.
.SS Architecture
The filesystem consists of three layers:
.IP \(bu 3
.B libmxfs
\(em portable C core library implementing XFS format I/O, DLM-aware
block/inode/directory caches, allocation, journaling, and cluster
services.
.IP \(bu 3
.B PAL
(Platform Abstraction Layer) \(em thin layer providing OS-specific
primitives (block I/O, threads, sockets, memory, time).
.IP \(bu 3
.B Linux VFS frontend
\(em translates VFS operations into libmxfs API calls.
.SS DLM Transports
MXFS supports two DLM (Distributed Lock Manager) transport backends:
.TP
.B CAW (Compare-And-Write)
Disk-based locking via SCSI Compare-And-Write operations.  No master
node \(em every node can acquire and release locks independently.
Scales to 64 nodes.  Requires storage that supports SCSI CAW (e.g.,
Linux LIO with
.BR emulate_caw=1 ).
.TP
.B TCP
Network-based locking with per-resource lock mastering.  Works with any
storage.  Recommended for up to 16 nodes (tested to 32).
.SS Three-Layer Fencing (CAW DLM only)
.IP 1. 3
.B SCSI-3 Persistent Reservations
\(em hardware-level access control on the shared block device.
.IP 2. 3
.B On-disk heartbeat
\(em per-node heartbeat sectors with ~62-second failure detection.
.IP 3. 3
.B DLM lock revocation
\(em stale locks from dead nodes are purged automatically.
.SS Features
.IP \(bu 3
Per-inode lock caching (locks held until BAST, eviction, or unmount)
.IP \(bu 3
AG (allocation group) affinity to minimize cross-node contention
.IP \(bu 3
Zero-config UDP multicast peer discovery (239.66.83.1:7601)
.IP \(bu 3
Per-node write-ahead journal with crash recovery
.IP \(bu 3
Extended attributes (xattrs)
.IP \(bu 3
POSIX ACLs
.IP \(bu 3
.BR fallocate (2)
.IP \(bu 3
.BR mmap (2)
.IP \(bu 3
.BR splice (2)
.IP \(bu 3
SEEK_HOLE / SEEK_DATA
.IP \(bu 3
Filesystem freeze/thaw for LVM snapshots
.IP \(bu 3
.BR sync (2)
/
.BR fsync (2)
.SH MOUNT OPTIONS
The following mount options are recognized by the
.B mxfs
filesystem type.  Options are specified as a comma-separated list
after the
.B \-o
flag.
.TP
.BI dlm_transport= transport
Set the DLM transport mode.  Valid values are:
.RS
.TP
.B auto
(Default.)  Auto-detect the transport.  Listen for peer discovery
announcements for 3 seconds.  If an existing cluster is found, adopt
that cluster's transport.  If no peers are found, probe the device for
SCSI CAW support \(em use CAW if supported, otherwise fall back to TCP.
.TP
.B caw
Force disk-based CAW DLM.  Requires SCSI Compare-And-Write support.
.TP
.B tcp
Force network-based TCP DLM.  SCSI Persistent Reservations are skipped.
.RE
.TP
.BI port= N
DLM TCP port number.  Default:
.BR 7600 .
Valid range: 1\(en65535.
.TP
.BI discovery_port= N
UDP discovery port number.  Default:
.BR 7601 .
Valid range: 1\(en65535.
.TP
.BI multicast= address
IPv4 multicast address for peer discovery.  Default:
.BR 239.66.83.1 .
.TP
.B broadcast
Use UDP broadcast instead of multicast for peer discovery.
.TP
.BI block_cache= N
Maximum number of cached disk blocks.  Default: auto-sized.
.TP
.BI inode_cache= N
Maximum number of cached inodes.  Default: auto-sized.
.TP
.BI dir_cache= N
Maximum number of cached directory entries.  Default: auto-sized.
.TP
.BI node_slot= N
Override automatic journal slot assignment.  Normally each node claims
a free journal slot on mount.  This option forces a specific slot.
.TP
.BI journal_offset= bytes
Override the journal region byte offset.  Normally read from the MXFS
on-disk superblock.  This option takes precedence.
.TP
.BI disklock_offset= bytes
Override the disklock region byte offset.  Normally read from the MXFS
on-disk superblock.  This option takes precedence.
.TP
.B noatime
Do not update inode access times on reads.  This is the
.B default
for MXFS, as atime updates on shared storage trigger journal
transactions and device flushes that cause significant read performance
regression.
.TP
.B relatime
Update atime only if it is older than mtime or ctime, or more than 24
hours old.  On MXFS, this option is treated as
.B noatime
for performance.  Use
.B strictatime
to force per-read atime updates.
.TP
.B nodiratime
Do not update directory access times.
.TP
.B strictatime
Update atime on every read.  Overrides the default noatime behavior.
Warning: may reduce read performance by up to 20% on shared storage.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/mxfs/node.uuid
Per-node UUID file.  If not present, a UUID is generated and written
on first mount.  Used to derive the 32-bit node ID via FNV-1a hash.
.TP
.I /etc/modules-load.d/mxfs.conf
Module auto-load configuration.  Contains "mxfs" to load the kernel
module at boot.
.TP
.I /usr/sbin/mkfs.mxfs
Filesystem format tool.
.TP
.I /usr/sbin/chk_mxfs
Filesystem integrity checker.
.TP
.I /usr/sbin/fsck.mxfs
Symlink to chk_mxfs for fstab fsck dispatch.
.TP
.I /usr/sbin/resize_mxfs
Filesystem resize tool.
.SH EXAMPLES
Format and mount a shared iSCSI LUN:
.PP
.RS
.nf
mkfs.mxfs /dev/sdb
insmod mxfs.ko
mount -t mxfs /dev/sdb /mnt/shared
.fi
.RE
.PP
Mount with TCP DLM transport (for storage without SCSI CAW):
.PP
.RS
.nf
mount -t mxfs -o dlm_transport=tcp /dev/sdb /mnt/shared
.fi
.RE
.PP
Mount with custom DLM port and discovery port:
.PP
.RS
.nf
mount -t mxfs -o port=9600,discovery_port=9601 /dev/sdb /mnt/shared
.fi
.RE
.PP
Add to
.I /etc/fstab
for automatic boot mount:
.PP
.RS
.nf
/dev/sdb  /mnt/shared  mxfs  _netdev  0  0
.fi
.RE
.PP
The
.B _netdev
option ensures the filesystem is mounted after network interfaces are
up, which is required for iSCSI devices and DLM networking.
.SH SUPPORTED STORAGE
Any shared block device accessible from all cluster nodes:
.IP \(bu 3
.B iSCSI
\(em tested with Linux LIO (CAW + TCP) and QNAP NAS (TCP only)
.IP \(bu 3
.B Fibre Channel
\(em any FC LUN with SCSI-3 PR support
.IP \(bu 3
.B NVMe-oF
\(em NVMe over Fabrics shared namespaces
.IP \(bu 3
.B SAS
\(em shared SAS enclosures
.SH KERNEL COMPATIBILITY
MXFS supports Linux kernels 5.x through 6.17 with compile-time version
guards for API differences.  Tested distributions include Debian 11/12/13,
Ubuntu 22.04/24.04, RHEL/AlmaLinux 9, and Proxmox VE 8.
